  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Logan Webb controlled this game from the first inning onward, and the lineup finally gave him what he needed.",
    "what_this_means": "They trailed after Colorado scored in the third, but the fourth inning unraveled the Rockies. Six runs poured across. Drew Gilbert's homer and two-out hitting made the difference. And that was the game. Webb allowed just one earned run across six innings while the relievers shut the door clean. Carson Seymour and Dylan Smith combined for three scoreless frames with three strikeouts, the kind of bullpen alignment that holds a lead without drama. This is what happens when the starter does his job and the bats convert runners in scoring position: they beat you 7-1 and it feels routine by the fifth.",
    "what_to_watch": "They won by controlling when it mattered most. Early, decisive, and held it tight the rest of the way.",
